# The M5 PR 12 pipped die, the other half of acceptance shape (v)
# (added to the CI-gated corpus by the M6 curation unit; M5 exit-walk
# row 12). A SHARP unit cube with 21 spherical dimples -- the classical
# layout, face n carrying n pips, opposite faces summing to seven --
# cut in ONE group subtraction. Six planar faces carrying rings whose
# carriers are exact circles, and 21 sphere bands (one per pip) as
# the dimple floors.
#
# Volume is the EXACT ANALYTIC value in FreeCAD's internal mm^3, not a
# readback: each ball (r = 0.09) sits r - h = 0.04 outside its face
# plane, so each dimple removes exactly a spherical cap of height
# h = 0.05, and V = 1 - 21*pi*h^2*(3r - h)/3 m^3.
#
# Kernel census is 27 faces / 54 edges / 50 vertices. OCC reports 75
# EDGES: on import it ADDS the DEGENERATE pole edge each sphere face
# needs in its own face model -- the same normalisation ball.expect
# records, at +1 per pip rather than +2, because a dimple is a cap and
# only ONE of its two poles survives the cut (21 * 1 = 21; 54 + 21 =
# 75). Faces, vertices and the volume are unchanged. These EXPECT_*
# counts were measured with OCC's own reader (the OCP bindings, as
# cone.expect says), not in FreeCAD itself.
#
# KERNEL_* pin the NATIVE body's census and certified volume, full
# precision (the literal is the export writer's round-tripping float
# printer's output; crates/step-export/tests/kernel_sidecars.rs asserts
# these lines against the live kernel). scripts/check_step.sh consumes
# EXPECT_* (what FreeCAD/OCC reports after import) and ignores KERNEL_*.
KERNEL_SOLIDS=1
KERNEL_SHELLS=1
KERNEL_FACES=27
KERNEL_EDGES=54
KERNEL_VERTICES=50
KERNEL_VOLUME_MM3=987904868.2836787
KERNEL_VOLUME_PAD_MM3=0.0
EXPECT_SOLIDS=1
EXPECT_SHELLS=1
EXPECT_FACES=27
EXPECT_EDGES=75
EXPECT_VERTICES=50
EXPECT_VOLUME_MM3=987904868.2836792
